This is Juggle, v1.0Juggle is a juggling animation program.  It can display *many*different juggling patterns.  You can specify the pattern for it todisplay, or tell it to pick a random one.At the moment, Juggle comes with a bog-standard curses display and aSilicon Graphics IRIS GL display - no X interface, I'm afraid (I don'thave time to learn X).  But it should be very easy to implement forsomeone who knows how - the graphics interface is all contained injuggle.h.  I'd appreciate a copy of an X interface if anyone doeswrite one.Juggle sprang up from a great article in a March '95 issue of NewScientist, by Ian Stewart.  The man page gives some of the detailsfrom that article.It's been tested on a DECstation (Ultrix) and a Silicon GraphicsIndigo (Irix).  To install, just customize the Makefile at the top andtype	install-bsd		if you're on a BSD-type system	install-sysv		if you're notThe next version (when I get around to it) will be able to switchjuggling patterns in mid-juggle - I think I've worked out thecondition for patterns to switch (the concatenation of the twopatterns must also be a valid pattern).Have fun with it.Glenn Hutchings                                                               __o                                zondo@hunting2.demon.co.uk   _`\<,_                                ............................(_)/ (_)